an retired files whose effect is absent from compiled state) or explicitly declare pre-existing laundered loss out of scope with rationale.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["E6","T4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Context: 'repairable damage silently becomes unrepairable-by-tooling loss at the first threshold crossing after the race. The existing repair door only works in the window BEFORE that fold.'","AC1 proves only the forward path (orphan kept, then repaired) — no AC covers a snapshot already laundered before the fix ships.","Out of scope enumerates G3, doctor, bridge/Jira, crash-atomicity, dirty-tree — but not already-laundered snapshots."],"finding":"The plan states the repair door 'only works in the window BEFORE that fold' and that laundering makes damage 'unrepairable-by-tooling loss at the first threshold crossing after the race.' The forward fix stops future laundering, but no acceptance criterion or scope item addresses tickets ALREADY laundered by a prior fold (retired+cited, effect-lost) — those remain unrepairable and undetected, and the plan neither includes a recovery/migration step nor explicitly declares such pre-existing damage out of scope.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdc8e9257ec398679","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Proposed fix / Acceptance criteria / Out of scope","norm_id":"n5388e836ef0117b6","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A deployment where a race + fold already happened before this fix lands: the orphan is already retired+cited, fsck reports clean, and this fix cannot recover it."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add an Out-of-scope bullet declaring pre-fix laundered snapshots unrecoverable-by-tooling (with rationale), OR add an AC/step for a diagnostic that flags retired+cited events whose effect is missing from compiled state.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"medium","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"hard","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the G1 exclusion predicate precisely: defer (leave unretired + un-cited) an old event ONLY when a PRIOR SNAPSHOT is present in the fold set, the event sorts before that snapshot, AND its uuid is absent from that prior snapshot's source_event_uuids — mirroring fsck_scan.py:381-386 — so the first-fold / no-prior-snapshot case cites and retires every event normally.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the natural fold (compact_txn) must EXCLUDE un-cited pre-snapshot events from both retirement and source_event_uuids citation'","compact_txn.py:507 sets snapshot_ts = max_old + 1 (after ALL folded events); :551-555 cites every non-SNAPSHOT old event — the fold CREATES the citation set, so 'cited' has no referent at fold time","fsck_scan.py:373-386 defines an orphan as an active event with name < snapshot_filename AND uuid not in source_uuid_set — i.e. relative to a specific SNAPSHOT already carrying source_event_uuids","_compact_locked reads no prior snapshot's source_event_uuids anywhere; the orphan signal it must reproduce depends on a PRIOR SNAPSHOT being present in the fold set (a re-compaction)","Prior review round already surfaced this exact gap (.rebar/cache/plan-review/f96b-3498-8f04-40b0/a98b...json) and the rewrite did not incorporate the fix"],"finding":"The G1 exclusion predicate 'EXCLUDE un-cited pre-snapshot events' is undefined at fold time and would misfire on a first (or prior-snapshot-free) fold. In compact_txn._compact_locked the new snapshot's timestamp is max_old+1, so every folded 'old' event is trivially pre-snapshot, and source_uuids is the citation list the fold is BUILDING — nothing is 'cited' yet. fsck's actual orphan signal (fsck_scan.py:381-386) is only well-defined relative to a PRIOR folded-in SNAPSHOT's source_event_uuids. The plan never anchors 'pre-snapshot'/'un-cited' to a prior snapshot present in the fold set, so a literal reading excludes ALL sources on a ticket's first compaction — breaking normal folds rather than only sparing genuine post-race orphans.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f27d1c775b739f46c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Proposed fix #1 / Scope: src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py","norm_id":"n967b0689a0841724","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A ticket crossing the compaction threshold for the FIRST time (no prior SNAPSHOT in the fold set): an over-broad 'un-cited pre-snapshot' predicate excludes every event from citation+retirement, yielding a degenerate/empty snapshot with all sources left live","A normal re-compaction where all pre-snapshot events ARE legitimately cited: without anchoring to the prior snapshot's cited set, the predicate cannot tell a genuine orphan from a normally-folded event"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State in Proposed fix #1 that the defer guard reads the source_event_uuids of any prior SNA